    {
      "id": "claim_47efb740adbc4e2aa93775537ff235cb",
      "statement": "Cross-trial and cross-agent are treated as distinct scope boundaries: cross-trial is a temporal boundary (same agent, separate invocations) while cross-agent is an identity boundary (distinct agents exchanging information via a protocol), narrowing the Macroatividade 2 confidentiality concern to handoffs between specialized agents within the same flow.",
